+
+**The minor blues.** A minor blues is the twelve-bar played in a minor key.
+*Walking bass over a minor 12-bar blues in C minor*, among this page's
+exercises, plays it one chord to a bar:
+
+- bars 1 to 4: Cm7, Cm7, Cm7, Cm7, that is i7 four times;
+- bars 5 to 8: Fm7, Fm7, Cm7, Cm7, that is iv7, iv7, i7, i7;
+- bars 9 to 12: A♭7, G7, Cm7, G7, that is ♭VI7, V7, i7, V7;
