+ * One row per fact the new text states. Each row reads the lesson's own sentence beside the fact, so neither side
+ * can move alone: the app's facts from the built content and `app/src` (`lessonClaimsAboutApp`'s three sources),
+ * the music from the built score files the learner opens. The three requirements the reviewer left open on this
+ * placement each have rows here:
+ *
+ * - `A7a3-minor-blues-source`: bars 9 and 10 taught as two variants, the generated items' ♭VI7-V7 and the Lab's
+ *   V7-iv7, each pinned against what that source actually plays, with no "standard" or "usually" claim;
+ * - `A7a3-stj-form-truth`: St. James Infirmary as a 16-bar verse and an 8-bar refrain, no repeat count and no
+ *   "three eight-bar phrases";
+ * - `A7a3-static-chart-feedback`: the last task with no Count off says the cell judges bar 1 only and is to be
+ *   ignored (the behaviour itself: `chordChart.test.ts`, "a chart that was never started judges bar 1 only").
+ *
+ * The walking pattern is pinned as this exercise's practice pattern, never as what a walking bass is. Nothing here
+ * was heard.
